exercises.solution:
```python
def approx_vertex_cover(edges):
    cover = set()
    for u, v in edges:
        if u not in cover and v not in cover:
            cover.add(u)
            cover.add(v)
    return cover
```

Every edge is either already covered when we reach it or becomes covered, so the result is a cover. The edges that triggered an addition form a matching $M$ (no two share a vertex), every cover needs a distinct vertex for each of them, and so $|\text{cover}| = 2|M| \le 2 \cdot \mathrm{OPT}$. It runs in $O(m)$ time with a hash set.

